      ":question/id": "01a0a2bd-671f-5194-8d72-321f7b00edef",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,y=\\frac{e^{t}}{6 t},\\,0<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=4.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=- \\frac{1}{2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}},\\,y'(t)=\\frac{6 t e^{t} - 6 e^{t}}{36 t^{2}}=\\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{6 t^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{6 t^{2}}\\cdot \\left(- 2 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{3 \\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=4,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =- \\frac{\\left(\\left(4\\right) - 1\\right) e^{\\left(4\\right)}}{3 \\sqrt{\\left(4\\right)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{- 3 e^{4}}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{e^{4}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
