      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3 \\sqrt{t}},\\,y=\\frac{e^{t}}{6 t},\\,0<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=3.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=- \\frac{1}{6 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}},\\,y'(t)=\\frac{6 t e^{t} - 6 e^{t}}{36 t^{2}}=\\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{6 t^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{6 t^{2}}\\cdot \\left(- 6 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{t}}{\\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=3,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =- \\frac{\\left(\\left(3\\right) - 1\\right) e^{\\left(3\\right)}}{\\sqrt{\\left(3\\right)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{- 2 e^{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3} e^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
